+    <p>
+      <strong>Brain helpers and optional transfers.</strong> Learned skills, workflow insights, and document records
+      are stored locally by default. The optional skill drafter can send one run's commands, file names, and a short
+      redacted error excerpt to your selected model provider when you allow it. In builds offering Codium Brain
+      helpers, a separate opt-in permits bounded excerpts from corrections, skill drafts, and selected document
+      sections to be sent through Codium to a qualified model with zero data retention. A subscription does not
+      enable that permission. Document suggestions require the document setting and an explicit request; Bootstrap
+      previews the documents and model before you confirm. Suggestions remain available for your review.
+    </p>
+    <p>
+      Brain attachment to GitHub runs started by the owner from the desktop and encrypted Brain Vault backup are
+      separate opt-in features, available only when the installed build and service offer their controls. Choosing an
+      attachment sends the selected context to that GitHub run. Choosing Vault sends an encrypted backup to the
+      selected backup service. Neither follows automatically from subscribing or allowing Codium Brain helpers.
+      Turning a helper off prevents new requests from that helper; it does not withdraw information already sent
+      to a model provider, GitHub run, or backup service.
+    </p>
